## Software design

> **Examples:** `../examples/software-design.php`

- **DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself):** Centralize logic and avoid duplicate code so that changes only need to be made in one place — in **any** language or layer (PHP services/controllers, Twig templates/components, CSS rule blocks, JavaScript modules). When two or more sites repeat the same block (≥5–10 substantially identical lines, or the same markup/logic with only names/ids differing), extract a shared function, private method, partial, component, macro, mixin, or utility class instead of copy-pasting.
- **KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid):** Systems work best when kept simple rather than complicated; always choose the simplest effective solution.
- **YAGNI (You Aren't Gonna Need It):** Do not add functionality or fancy features until they are strictly necessary.
- **Separation of Concerns:** Divide a program into distinct sections where each addresses a separate, distinct concern or feature set — including **passive DTOs vs persistence** (`persistResult()` on a class in `src/Dto/` mixes data transfer with Doctrine unit-of-work).
- **Single Responsibility Principle (SRP):** A class should only have one reason to change — it should do one specific job.
- **Modularity:** Break down large, complex systems into smaller, independent, and interchangeable components.
- **Abstraction:** Hide complex implementation details and expose only the relevant, high-level features — callers should not need transport, storage, or integration identifiers in method names; keep **how/where/why** inside the adapter the method delegates to.
- **Encapsulation:** Bundle data and the methods that operate on it within one unit; restrict direct access to internal components.
- **Maintain One Source of Truth:** Avoid duplicating state or data across different locations to prevent sync bugs.
- **One variable, one meaning:** Do not overload a single field or variable with two independent facts (e.g. nullable `items` meaning both “no data yet” and “operation not complete”, or `null` hiding a partial list while a separate boolean already exists). Use an explicit flag (`isReady`, `doAllHaveOutcome`), a discriminated result type, or separate return paths — in PHP DTOs, JavaScript modules, and API payloads alike.
